04825318232178688,-0.0016737689729779959,-0.0920189619064331,-0.08616827428340912,-0.010706648230552673,-0.05124754458665848,-0.06178627163171768,-0.062410127371549606,0.04126715287566185,0.09691089391708374,0.026469329372048378,0.059076275676488876,0.038983430713415146,-0.03895954042673111,0.04636477306485176,-0.032598063349723816,0.04211805760860443,0.055394355207681656,0.012414365075528622,0.06367526203393936]},{"id":"privacy-notice-01","source":"privacy-notice.txt","index":1,"section":"3. WHAT WE COLLECT › 3.2 Information collected automatically","sections":["3. WHAT WE COLLECT › 3.2 Information collected automatically","4. HOW WE USE IT","5. WHO CAN SEE IT","5. WHO CAN SEE IT › 5.1 Other collectors","5. WHO CAN SEE IT › 5.2 Admins and support staff","5. WHO CAN SEE IT › 5.3 Service providers"],"words":386,"overlapWords":0,"text":"3.2 Information collected automatically\n\n- Server logs. For every request we record the page or API route (the path only, never the part after \"?\"), the method, the response status and how long it took. Search requests also record the question you typed and how many results came back. Errors are recorded with a short error code. - Log protection. The logger removes values whose names suggest secrets, such as passwords, tokens, cookies, session IDs, API keys, email addresses, request bodies, card numbers and database connection details, before anything is written. - Analytics. We use Vercel Web Analytics to count page views and visitors. [TO CONFIRM: confirm with the provider's current documentation that this is cookie-free and does not store IP addresses.] - Test user choice. A cookie remembers which test user you picked.\n\nWe do not collect payment card details, bank details, precise location, contacts, or photos. (Card photos are planned but not built.)\n\n4. HOW WE USE IT\n\n- To run the Application: show your collection, find wishlist matches, record trades and produce your reports. - To protect serial numbers and resolve serial-number conflicts. - To answer support requests and investigate trade disputes. - To keep the Application secure and fix errors. - To understand which pages are used, so we can improve them.\n\nWe do not sell your personal information, and we do not use it for advertising.\n\n5. WHO CAN SEE IT\n\n5.1 Other collectors\n\nOther collectors can see:\n\n- your username; - your tradeable cards, including grade, serial number and cert number; - your public wants.\n\nThey cannot see your paid prices, listed prices, acquired dates, private wants, non-tradeable cards or sold records. Only the two collectors in a trade can see that trade and its message.\n\nWhen a card moves to another collector through a trade, your paid and listed prices are removed from it, and its acquired date is reset.\n\n5.2 Admins and support staff\n\nAdmins can see all collection data. They use it only to resolve serial-number conflicts and support requests. Support staff look at your data only to answer your request.\n\n5.3 Service providers\n\nWe use these providers to run the Application. Each processes data only on our instructions:\n\n- Vercel: hosting, server logs and web analytics. - Neon: the Postgres database where Application data is stored.","tokens":499,"embedding":[-0.1156500056385994,0.0827542394399643,-0.1310870498418808,0.019858073443174362,-0.011441108770668507,-0.06956173479557037,0.07912637293338776,0.01586919091641903,0.04289279505610466,0.030445042997598648,0.012000445276498795,0.010711424052715302,0.046582192182540894,-0.05370485037565231,-0.051215071231126785,-0.037189166992902756,0.026262803003191948,-0.009335345588624477,-0.08420033007860184,-0.02131972275674343,0.01869421824812889,-0.030524445697665215,-0.024272529408335686,0.025296635925769806,-0.07239942997694016,-0.014497273601591587,-0.06414434313774109,-0.020535459741950035,-0.06587665528059006,-0.0634598582983017,-0.04382787644863129,0.06877207010984421,-0.014880704693496227,0.08572865277528763,-0.058274101465940475,-