 your search question is not sent to an outside AI service. A separate developer tool can send questions and reference-document passages to Anthropic's Claude model, but it is not part of the web Application and never sends collection data. [TO CONFIRM provider list before publication.]\n\n5.4 When the law requires it\n\nWe may share information if the law requires it, or to protect the safety of collectors or the public.\n\n6. HOW LONG WE KEEP IT\n\n- Collection, wishlist and trade data: while your account is open. - Trade records involving another collector: kept after you leave, with your details removed, so the other collector's history stays accurate. - Catalog entries: kept as part of the shared catalog, without your name. - Server logs: [TO CONFIRM, for example 30 days]. - Support conversations: [TO CONFIRM, for example 2 years]. - Test environments: may be reset at any time.\n\n7. HOW WE PROTECT IT\n\n- Database row-level security, so each collector can change only their own cards and wants, and can see only trades they are part of. - Encrypted connections to the database, with the server certificate checked. - Error messages never show database host or account details. - Development tools refuse to run against the production database.\n\nSee the Security and Incident Response document (security-incident-response.txt) for more, including what we do if data is exposed.\n\n8. YOUR CHOICES AND RIGHTS\n\n- Make a want private by unticking \"Public\". - Turn a card's Tradeable setting off to hide it from other collectors. - Ask us for a copy of your data. - Ask us to correct your data. - Ask us to delete your account and collection.\n\nWe confirm your identity first and complete requests within 30 days. Depending on where you live, you may have further rights, including the right to complain to a data protection authority. [TO CONFIRM by jurisdiction]","tokens":465,"embedding":[-0.0819200798869133,0.04778179153800011,-0.13454124331474304,0.029607534408569336,-0.0